{"type":"message","id":"72287336","parentId":"6d11ec98","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:46:26.189Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass.\n\n**Cause:** the format string `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"` has nothing to match the `Z` at the end of `2026-10-12T08:30:00Z`, so `strptime` raised the error.\n\n**Fix:** `parse_date` now calls `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime`.\n- Timestamps ending in `Z` or an offset like `+02:00` now return timezone-aware datetimes. They keep the UTC/offset information instead of dropping it.\n- Timestamps without a timezone still return plain (naive) datetimes, so `test_naive` and `day_key` behave as before.\n- It also accepts other valid ISO-8601 forms, such as fractional seconds, which the old code rejected.\n\n**Things to check:**\n- Code that compares results or does date arithmetic with them could now mix aware and naive datetimes, which raises `TypeError`. If you'd rather always get naive datetimes, add `.replace(tzinfo=None)`.\n- `fromisoformat` only accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 or later. The tests ran on 3.13.5; on older versions you'd need to replace the `Z` yourself before parsing."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":445,"cacheRead":25495,"cacheWrite":1378,"totalTokens":27320,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":1378}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277180777,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8d1zUqmSkgZuM5r5K8u","duration":5404.458674000001,"ttft":5387.251770999999,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26875,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
